The `denoising/` and `diffusion/` packages are an adapted, renamed fork of:

  HI-Diff: Hierarchical Integration Diffusion Model for Realistic Image Deblurring
  Zheng Chen, Yulun Zhang, Ding Liu, Bin Xia, Jinjin Gu, Linghe Kong, Xin Yuan
  NeurIPS 2023 (Spotlight)
  https://github.com/zhengchen1999/HI-Diff
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

HI-Diff itself is built on and/or references the following Apache-2.0 licensed projects:

  BasicSR
  https://github.com/XPixelGroup/BasicSR

  Restormer: Efficient Transformer for High-Resolution Image Restoration
  Syed Waqas Zamir, Aditya Arora, Salman Khan, Munawar Hayat, Fahad Shahbaz Khan, Ming-Hsuan Yang
  https://github.com/swz30/Restormer

  DiffIR: Efficient Diffusion Model for Image Restoration
  Bin Xia, Yulun Zhang, Shiyin Wang, Yitong Wang, Xinglong Wu, Yapeng Tian, Wenming Yang, Luc Van Gool
  https://github.com/Zj-BinXia/DiffIR

  MambaIR / MambaIRv2: State Space Model for Image Restoration
  https://github.com/csguoh/MambaIR

`scripts/evaluate_realblur.py` and `scripts/generate_patches_gopro.py` are adapted from:

  Restormer: Efficient Transformer for High-Resolution Image Restoration
  https://github.com/swz30/Restormer

`evaluate/NIQA/` bundles several no-reference IQA implementations (BRISQUE, NIQE, PIQE,
RankIQA, MetaIQA) adapted from third-party sources; see `evaluate/NIQA/readme.md` for the
full per-component attribution.

See each project's repository for its full license text and citation details.
